WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.580 --> 00:00:04.720
Perhaps it's a reflection of the unstable
times in which we find ourselves, but 2018

00:00:04.720 --> 00:00:06.960
has been an intense year at the movies.

00:00:07.029 --> 00:00:11.900
From a harrowing bit of pulpy detective fiction
to a bloody tale of revenge, and all manner

00:00:11.900 --> 00:00:16.400
of nervy narratives in between, these are
the most disturbing movies of 2018.

00:00:17.400 --> 00:00:21.510
Indie director Lynne Ramsay knocked audiences
off their feet when she unleashed You Were

00:00:21.510 --> 00:00:23.240
Never Really Here in the spring.

00:00:23.449 --> 00:00:27.779
The movie is a frenzied, bloody, deeply paranoid
fever dream of a film that's anchored by a

00:00:27.779 --> 00:00:30.250
passionate performance from Joaquin Phoenix.

00:00:30.250 --> 00:00:34.270
The film hammers its way into your head like
a nightmare incarnate, one you won't easily

00:00:34.270 --> 00:00:34.960
wake from.

00:00:35.280 --> 00:00:36.440
"McCleary said you were brutal."

00:00:41.340 --> 00:00:42.280
"I can be."

00:00:43.600 --> 00:00:47.530
The kids are not alright in Thoroughbreds,
a movie which follows two upper-class teens

00:00:47.530 --> 00:00:52.280
who live on opposite ends of the human emotional
spectrum, one incapable of feeling anything,

00:00:52.280 --> 00:00:53.800
while the other feels everything.

00:00:53.840 --> 00:00:58.420
When they're reunited after years apart, each
finds themselves hatching a violent plan to

00:00:58.420 --> 00:01:00.980
take control of their rapidly spiraling lives.

00:01:01.160 --> 00:01:06.360
Director Cory Finley wisely allows the crime
itself to play second fiddle throughout Thoroughbreds,

00:01:06.360 --> 00:01:09.700
focusing instead on the tragically inventive
young minds behind it.

00:01:09.820 --> 00:01:12.280
That choice lands some of Thoroughbreds' biggest
laughs.

00:01:12.280 --> 00:01:16.550
It also lends an exacting edge to the film's
final moments, which may leave you giggling

00:01:16.550 --> 00:01:19.200
while also fighting a nasty chill in your
spine.

00:01:19.960 --> 00:01:24.820
With its politically charged narrative of
societal despair, environmental calamity,

00:01:24.830 --> 00:01:29.550
and righteous indignation, First Reformed
is a film unmistakably of the times.

00:01:29.550 --> 00:01:33.750
The film stars Ethan Hawke as a troubled,
well-intentioned priest in a world where moral

00:01:33.750 --> 00:01:39.030
duplicity has led to big business corrupting
not just society, but also the environment

00:01:39.030 --> 00:01:39.880
and the church.

00:01:40.170 --> 00:01:45.560
First Reformed is a devastating desolate piece
of work driven by insightful writing, unforgettable

00:01:45.560 --> 00:01:49.460
imagery, and an atmospheric energy that teeters
ever on the edge of horror.

00:01:50.340 --> 00:01:55.031
Part nerve-wracking survival story and part
full-tilt tale of righteous vengeance, Revenge

00:01:55.031 --> 00:01:58.090
unfolds in the suffocating heat of a sun-bleached
valley.

00:01:58.090 --> 00:02:02.190
The film follows a pampered American party
girl named Jen who is left for dead in the

00:02:02.190 --> 00:02:05.420
unforgiving desert following a horrific act
of violence.

00:02:05.420 --> 00:02:09.580
Instead of dying though, Jen wakes up, and
heads off to exact some violent revenge in

00:02:09.580 --> 00:02:12.400
bloody and inventive ways that we won't spoil.

00:02:12.440 --> 00:02:16.940
Just know that the final showdown will leave
you gasping, clapping, and absolutely shaken

00:02:16.940 --> 00:02:17.640
to the core.

00:02:18.610 --> 00:02:22.100
For those who haven't seen Hereditary, the
less you know going in the better, but we

00:02:22.110 --> 00:02:26.720
can say that this film begins in a dark, tense
place that sends audiences into one of the

00:02:26.720 --> 00:02:29.180
most shocking moments in horror movie history.

00:02:29.400 --> 00:02:32.840
If you've seen Hereditary, you know exactly
we're talking about.

00:02:32.840 --> 00:02:37.230
If not, well, we both pity and envy the fact
that you've yet to experience that moment

00:02:37.230 --> 00:02:39.180
in all of its trauma-inducing horror.

00:02:39.370 --> 00:02:43.020
If you're tough enough to stick with it, you'll
be able to brag to friends that you made it

00:02:43.020 --> 00:02:46.400
through one of the best, most disturbing horror
films of 2018.

00:02:46.400 --> 00:02:48.540
"Don't you swear at me you little s---.

00:02:48.920 --> 00:02:51.060
Don't you ever raise your voice at me.

00:02:51.060 --> 00:02:52.080
I am your mother!

00:02:52.800 --> 00:02:53.900
Do you understand?"

00:02:55.180 --> 00:03:00.220
A uniquely disquieting movie, Mandy combines
grindhouse violence and an unhinged performance

00:03:00.220 --> 00:03:02.220
from Nicholas Cage to perfect effect.

00:03:02.280 --> 00:03:07.080
The movie is packed to the brim with a dangerous
cult of hippies, a demonic biker gang, copious

00:03:07.080 --> 00:03:12.140
amounts of hallucinations, intensely surrealistic
imagery, and enough fake blood to float an

00:03:12.140 --> 00:03:12.640
ark.

00:03:12.640 --> 00:03:16.940
There's also a chainsaw fight that instantly
earned Mandy a spot in the vault of cult classics.

00:03:17.160 --> 00:03:21.980
Yes, Mandy is every bit the B-movie it seems,
but it's also one of the most visually striking

00:03:21.989 --> 00:03:27.040
and wholly original films of the year, and
its unbridled insanity simply must be seen

00:03:27.040 --> 00:03:27.780
to be believed.

00:03:29.160 --> 00:03:32.460
From its jarring opening moments, Like Me
is clearly out to shock.

00:03:32.640 --> 00:03:37.040
The film follows a woman broadcasting her
own crime spree across social media.

00:03:37.180 --> 00:03:42.480
Part road movie, part hallucinatory crime
thriller, and part isolationist chamber drama,

00:03:42.489 --> 00:03:46.580
it opens with an attention-grabbing heist
and ends with a brutal act of violence.

00:03:46.580 --> 00:03:51.280
The moments in between find the film skillfully
laying the groundwork for a character study

00:03:51.280 --> 00:03:55.620
uniquely tuned in to the emptiness that accompanies
a life lived on social media.

00:03:55.700 --> 00:04:00.540
The film's vivid photography and crazy editing
ensure that even its muted moments come and

00:04:00.540 --> 00:04:02.230
go with galvanizing energy.

00:04:02.230 --> 00:04:07.019
That manic mix of styles makes Like Me the
sort of soul-crushingly spirited film you

00:04:07.020 --> 00:04:07.860
need to see.

00:04:08.700 --> 00:04:13.800
For the uninitiated, Unsane follows a woman
who, in seeking help for her emotional problems

00:04:13.800 --> 00:04:16.660
inadvertently commits herself to a mental
institution.

00:04:16.800 --> 00:04:21.240
Worse, she finds that it's a lot easier to
get into a mental institution than it is to

00:04:21.240 --> 00:04:21.820
get out.

00:04:21.820 --> 00:04:26.560
Making matters somehow even worse is the appearance
of the super creepy stalker she's been in

00:04:26.560 --> 00:04:29.700
hiding from, who might just be a figment of
her imagination.

00:04:29.700 --> 00:04:35.920
From that setup, Unsane becomes a moody, obsessive
little film that features a stalker, a PTSD-suffering

00:04:35.930 --> 00:04:38.909
heroine, and some shockingly gory violence.

00:04:38.909 --> 00:04:43.069
What makes the film so scary is just how plausible
all the inherent insanity seems.

00:04:43.069 --> 00:04:47.550
At the very least, Unsane will have you reading
every single word of fine print on the next

00:04:47.550 --> 00:04:48.740
document you sign.

00:04:48.760 --> 00:04:50.540
"Are you refusing to cooperate?"

00:04:51.380 --> 00:04:52.680
"What happens if I do?"

00:04:53.340 --> 00:04:57.620
"It would be better for everyone but especially
yourself if you just do as I ask."

